{
  "_spdx": "SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Wisbendji Fimerlus <archledger236@gmail.com>; SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later",
  "_comment": "Plasma Fusion performance budget, BACKLOG section 7 (2026-09-30-research/BACKLOG.md). Lower is better for every metric. 'budget' holds the limit per geometry (virtual output size in device px @ scale; 'default' is the 1440x900 value, used when section 7 gives one value); 'noise' is the regression margin against the stored baseline: a run regresses when its median exceeds the baseline's maximum by more than max(abs, rel * baseline median). Margins come from the spread of the perf-measure A/B runs (n=4 per arm). The idle rows have wide margins while the round-2 system card is on the desktop: it redraws on every 2 s update and glides (14 frames) when a bar moves 3 px or more, so its idle cost follows the host's own CPU and memory activity (1.2-5.9 frames/s measured on one build); one glide more per 30 s is 0.47 frames/s. Tighten them after BACKLOG M5.",
